  "report_period": "Week 32 (2nd Aug to 9th Aug 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Wilmar International committed their Kamsarmax \"Theresa Guangdong\" 81/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS 05/2027, DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) and the sisters \"Theresa Hebei\" & \"Theresa Jilin\" 81/2012 Sainty, China (SS 03/2027, DD 04/2025 & SS 06/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) to clients of Fujian Highton at USD 19,2 mill each. For reference, the \"Yu Qiang\" 81/2012 PLA 4807, China (SS 05/2027, DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 17,5 mill. The Ultramax \"Dolce Vita\" 61/2012 Oshima, Japan (SS 09/2027, DD 01/2026, BWTS fitted) of Drydel Shipping was committed to Chinese interests at USD 23,5 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel \"Ultra Rocanville\" 61/2012 Oshima, Japan (SS 03/2027, DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in early May at low USD 23 mill. On the Supramax sector, Santoku Senpaku committed their OHBS \"Suzaku\" 54/2006 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 07/2026, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1C) at mid USD 14 mill. Moreover, Hubei Qintai Shipping committed their \"Monica D\" 52/2001 Shin Kurushima, Japan (SS 12/2026, DD 12/2024) at USD 7,8 mill. Remind you that three months ago, the \"Sonya Blade\" 52/2001 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 10/2026, DD 08/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 8,3 mill. Inui Global Logistics committed the OHBS Handysize \"Ken Ryu\" 31/2002 Saiki, Japan (SS 06/2027, DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) to Chinese interests at USD 6,8 mill. Note that a month ago, the sister vessel \"HG Darwin\" 31/2002 Saiki, Japan (SS 04/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted, OHBS) was sold at USD 8,2 mill.",
    "tankers": "The VLCC \"Apollo Harmony\" 301/2010 IHI, Japan (SS/DD 03/2025, BWTS fitted) of Idemitsu Tanker was committed on subs to Greek interests at region USD 58 mill. For reference, the one-year-older Korean built \"C. Prosperity\" 313/2009 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 08/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold in late June at USD 53,5 mill. Navios committed their MR2 \"Nave Orbit\" 50/2009 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 10/2024, BWTS fitted) to undisclosed interests at USD 25,9 mill basis forward delivery. Remind you that a couple of months ago, the sister vessel \"Gunmetal Jack\" 50/2009 Spp, Korea (SS 08/2029, DD 05/2027, BWTS fitted) was sold at excess USD 28 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 12,000/15,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 10,000/13,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level 17,000/19,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 700K/900K. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 21,000/22,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 11,000/13,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd. Indian Coastal trips were fixed around usd 9,000/10,000 pd. Indian trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd. South African trips into India were reported at the level of usd 20,000/22,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were fixed around usd 23,000/27,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of trips from China into Continent were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips were reported at the level of usd 8,000/10,000 pd. Continental trips into South America were fixed around usd 7,000/8,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 18,000/21,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
